1
00:04:28,695 --> 00:04:34,695
Forced to host the enemy. Tormented by intruders. Tempted by desire.

2
00:08:57,391 --> 00:09:03,391
Suite Française is a drama, romance, war film directed by Saul Dibb.

3
00:13:26,086 --> 00:13:32,086
France, 1940.

4
00:17:54,782 --> 00:18:00,782
In the first days of occupation, beautiful Lucile Angellier is trapped in a stifled existence with her
controlling mother-in-law as they both await news of her husband: a prisoner of war.

5
00:22:23,478 --> 00:22:29,478
Parisian refugees start to pour into their small town, soon followed by a regiment of
German soldiers who take up residence in the villagers' own homes.

6
00:26:52,173 --> 00:26:58,173
Lucile initially tries to ignore Bruno von Falk, the handsome
and refined German officer staying with them.

7
00:31:20,869 --> 00:31:26,869
But soon, a powerful love draws them together and
leads them into the tragedy of war.

8
00:35:49,565 --> 00:35:55,565
Lucille Angellier, played by Michelle Williams.

9
00:40:18,260 --> 00:40:24,260
Madame Angellier, played by Kristin Scott Thomas.

10
00:44:46,956 --> 00:44:52,956
Lieutenant Bruno Von Falk, played by Matthias Schoenaerts.

11
00:49:15,652 --> 00:49:21,652
Benoit Labarie, played by Sam Riley.

12
00:53:44,347 --> 00:53:50,347
Madeleine Labarie, played by Ruth Wilson.

13
00:58:13,043 --> 00:58:19,043
Major, played by Heino Ferch.

14
01:02:41,739 --> 01:02:47,739
Suite Française is a 2015 war romantic drama film directed by
Saul Dibb and co-written with Matt Charman.

15
01:07:10,434 --> 01:07:16,434
It is based on the second part of Irène
Némirovsky's 2004 novel of the same name.

16
01:11:39,130 --> 01:11:45,130
The film stars Michelle Williams, Kristin Scott Thomas, Matthias
Schoenaerts, Sam Riley, Ruth Wilson, Lambert Wilson and Margot Robbie.

17
01:16:07,826 --> 01:16:13,826
It concerns a romance between a French villager and a German soldier during the
early years of the German occupation of France during World War II.

18
01:20:36,521 --> 01:20:42,521
Suite Française was filmed on location in France and Belgium.

19
01:25:05,217 --> 01:25:11,217
It was released theatrically in the UK on 13 March 2015 and premiered in
the US through Lifetime cable network on 22 May 2017.

20
01:29:33,913 --> 01:29:39,913
The film was nominated for a Primetime Emmy Award
for Outstanding Music Composition.

21
01:34:02,608 --> 01:34:08,608
The film explores themes of based on novel or book, world war ii,
prisoner of war, forbidden love, french resistance.

22
01:38:31,304 --> 01:38:37,304
The tone is emotional.
